 * kernel-self.compact — ContractAddress bytes are a field, not a Kernel method.
 *
 * Official reads (not invented APIs):
 *   kernel.self(): ContractAddress
 *     https://docs.midnight.network/compact/data-types/ledger-adt
 *   struct ContractAddress { bytes: Bytes<32>; }
 *     https://docs.midnight.network/compact/standard-library/exports
 *   kernel.self() example:
 *     https://docs.midnight.network/compact/reference/compact-reference
 *   MerkleTree.insert(item) inserts one leaf:
 *     https://docs.midnight.network/compact/data-types/ledger-adt
 *   emit in a constructor is a static error:
 *     https://docs.midnight.network/compact/reference/compact-reference
 *
 * Upstream: midnightntwrk/midnight-docs#1387
 * Kapa could not answer whether kernel.self().bytes exists. It does, as a
 * field read on the ContractAddress returned by kernel.self(). kernel.bytes
 * is not a documented Kernel operation. MerkleTree.insert takes one leaf.
 *
 * Language pin: Compact ~0.31.1 / language ~0.23.
